    "title": "<p>Proposed algorithms for stratifying the behaviour of uterine perivascular epithelioid cell tumours (PEComas); a proposal based on synthesis of information from the three sources cited below; the mitotic count threshold equates to 1&nbsp;mitosis in 50&nbsp;high-power fields (HPF) of diameter 0.55&nbsp;mm, area 0.24&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup></p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Jennifer A. Bennett",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"width: 703.3pt; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 91.3pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"122\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 306.0pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"408\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>General criteria<br /></strong><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{16327428}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 306.0pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"408\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Modified gynaecology-specific criteria<br /></strong><span class=\"Ref-PMID\">{24418852; 30001237}</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 91.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"122\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Benign</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 306.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"408\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&lt;&nbsp;5&nbsp;cm, non-infiltrative, non-high nuclear grade, mitotic count of &le;&nbsp;1&nbsp;mitosis/12 mm<sup>2</sup>, no necrosis, no vascular invasion</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 306.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"408\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 91.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"122\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Uncertain malignant potential</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 306.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"408\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Nuclear pleomorphism&nbsp;/ multinucleated giant cells or &gt;&nbsp;5&nbsp;cm</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 306.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"408\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&lt;&nbsp;3&nbsp;of the following features: &ge;&nbsp;5&nbsp;cm, high nuclear grade, mitotic count of &gt;&nbsp;1&nbsp;mitosis/12 mm<sup>2</sup>, necrosis, vascular invasion</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 91.3pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"122\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Malignant</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 306.0pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"408\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&ge;&nbsp;2&nbsp;of the following features: &gt;&nbsp;5&nbsp;cm, infiltrative, high nuclear grade, mitotic count of &gt;&nbsp;1&nbsp;mitosis/12 mm<sup>2</sup>, necrosis, vascular invasion</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 306.0pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"408\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&ge;&nbsp;3&nbsp;features</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
